{
  "wasim_version": "0.1.0",
  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Arithmetic-average Asian call priced by path Monte Carlo, with the geometric-average Asian as a control variate (Glasserman, Sec 1.1.2 / Eq 3.28 Asian payoff; geometric control is the textbook reducer, Sec 4.1). GBM path via a process node driving an accumulator (exact GBM per step). The average is taken over the monitoring points captured by running sums, with the count from a step-counter accumulator so the average is self-consistent under the engine's one-step stock-read lag. The geometric Asian has a closed form (Kemna-Vorst, live via erf) that is BOTH the validation reference and the control's known mean. Run results_spec.final_stats on payoff_arith / cv_arith / geo_price. See ASIAN_OPTION_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
